{
  "README": [
    "NCEI U.S. Climate Normals 1991-2020 \u2014 annual/seasonal freeze-date probabilities (seed table).",
    "Every value below was parsed from an actually-fetched per-station NCEI normals CSV; no value is estimated or hand-entered.",
    "Canonical source per station: https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/data/normals-annualseasonal/1991-2020/access/<STATION_ID>.csv (recorded per station as sourceUrl).",
    "Fetched via NOAA's official Open Data Dissemination mirror of the same files, https://noaa-normals-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/normals-annualseasonal/1991-2020/access/<STATION_ID>.csv (recorded per station as fetchedFrom), because direct ncei.noaa.gov egress was blocked in the build environment. The bucket is NOAA-operated (https://registry.opendata.aws/noaa-climate-normals/).",
    "Column -> value mapping: the CSV has one data row per station. Freeze-date probability columns are named ANN-TMIN-PRBLST-T<T>FP<P> (last spring occurrence of a minimum <= T degF, exceedance probability P%) and ANN-TMIN-PRBFST-T<T>FP<P> (first fall occurrence), for T in {36,32,28,24,20,16} and P in {90..10}. Values are whitespace-padded 'MM/DD' calendar-date strings (e.g. ' 03/31'); missing values are blank or negative sentinels and are OMITTED here, never invented.",
    "Encoding here: lastFrost/firstFrost maps keyed by FrostKey '<thresholdF>/<probabilityPct>' (schema/types.ts), value = day-of-year 1..365 on the engine's non-leap calendar (MM/DD converted with month lengths 31,28,31,30,31,30,31,31,30,31,30,31 \u2014 matches calendarDayOfYear in schema/engine/resolve.ts).",
    "Semantics: lastFrost['32/50'] is the 50%-probability date of the last spring 32 degF freeze ('or later'); firstFrost['32/50'] the 50%-probability first fall freeze ('or earlier'). In warm climates the 'first fall' freeze can fall in January of the following calendar year (e.g. Phoenix firstFrost 32/50 = day 3), so firstFrost may be numerically smaller than lastFrost; frost-free-day arithmetic must wrap (see buildSiteContext).",
    "Station id/name/lat/lng come verbatim from the STATION/NAME/LATITUDE/LONGITUDE columns of the same CSV.",
    "Stations attempted but excluded (honesty rule - no fabrication): USW00012839 (Miami Intl AP, FL) - its CSV contains no freeze-date probability values at any threshold."
  ],
